  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"114\" data-end=\"311\"><strong data-start=\"114\" data-end=\"134\">Fluid creatinine</strong> measurement is primarily used to differentiate between various types of body fluid accumulations, especially to <strong data-start=\"247\" data-end=\"273\">identify urine leakage</strong> (urinoma) into body cavities such as:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"313\" data-end=\"446\">\n<li data-start=\"313\" data-end=\"385\">\n<p data-start=\"315\" data-end=\"385\"><strong data-start=\"315\" data-end=\"336\">Peritoneal cavity</strong> (e.g., after bladder rupture or ureteral injury)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"386\" data-end=\"418\">\n<p data-start=\"388\" data-end=\"418\"><strong data-start=\"388\" data-end=\"405\">Pleural space</strong> (rare cases)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"419\" data-end=\"446\">\n<p data-start=\"421\" data-end=\"446\"><strong data-start=\"421\" data-end=\"446\">Retroperitoneal space</strong></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"448\" data-end=\"540\">The test is most commonly used when <strong data-start=\"484\" data-end=\"503\">urinous ascites</strong> or <strong data-start=\"507\" data-end=\"526\">urinary fistula</strong> is suspected.</p>\n<p data-start=\"448\" data-end=\"540\">Elevated creatinine levels in body fluid&mdash;especially when compared to serum creatinine&mdash;are <strong data-start=\"689\" data-end=\"735\">highly suggestive of urinary tract leakage</strong>. Specifically:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Condition</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Significance</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Bladder rupture or injury</strong></td>\n<td>Urine leaks into the peritoneal cavity, raising fluid creatinine levels significantly</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Ureteric injury post-surgery</strong></td>\n<td>Results in retroperitoneal urinoma or urinary ascites</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Vesicoperitoneal fistula</strong></td>\n<td>Connects bladder to peritoneal space, causing elevated fluid creatinine</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p data-start=\"448\" data-end=\"540\">&nbsp;</p>",
